WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:01.840
When the old blood was found

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:04.120
it must have been thought a miracle.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.560
They called it "the blood of the Gods"

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.560
and rightly so

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.320
for if you injected it into your veins

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.800
you would no longer be afflicted by the weaknesses of the flesh.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.680
it follows that a city built upon this blood would become mighty indeed

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.680
and so it was with Yharnam.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.360
The supply of the blood was controlled by the Healing Church

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.280
and the Church became the most powerful of all.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.500
But the blood was foul, infected.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.920
Those who've taken the old blood began transforming into hideous beasts

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.760
and eventually, the Church could keep the scourge a secret no longer.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.780
Fearing the populace itself

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.900
they retreated into Cathedral Ward

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.240
and devised a plan to fight back.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.360
The Church Hunters were that plan.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:52.600
The hunters in white specialized in experimental blood ministration

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.800
for the Church continued to use the old blood.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.360
Albeit now, with fear in their hearts.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.300
The hunters in black were a little different,

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:05.080
their role was to violently purge this town of the beastly scourge.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.420
Beasthood was a cancer

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.420
and with their surgical white gloves

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:13.660
the black Church Hunters would rip the beasthood from the hearts of the yharnamites.

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:16.200
They were known to dispose the victims,

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.660
even potential victims,

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:21.360
before signs of sickness had even manifested themselves.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.700
Their black attire inspired fear in the hearts of the Yharnamites

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.500
for if they decided that you had the beast within you,

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:30.760
then it was so.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.600
But the beast lies dormant within us all.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:39.160
And ironically, the clerics transformed into the most terrifying beasts.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:43.200
"Father" is a title used for clerics in a foreign land

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.640
and the Healing Church knew no such rank.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:50.960
An outsider, Father Gascoigne, joined the ranks of the Black Church Hunters

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:54.400
Perhaps he, like many others, was sick

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:55.940
and needed treatment.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:59.180
Perhaps he saw the miracles that the Church was performing.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:00.980
Actual miracles

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:03.440
that could've inspired a new faith in the men.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.340
Or perhaps it was thirst for blood that drew him here

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.400
for Gascoigne turned out to be a truly capable hunter.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.480
A fine addition to the ranks of the Church.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:17.060
Gascoigne was partnered with another,

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:19.620
an older hunter, by the name of Henryk.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.620
Capable, beyond his years.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:26.580
This old man was easily recognizable in his unique yellow garb.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:31.340
It's description tells us that they were a fierce and gallant duo,

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:36.320
but also that their partnership led to Henryk's tragically long life.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:38.680
He must have been very old indeed

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.680
to be tragically so.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.940
Perhaps Gascoigne's access to the Church

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:45.600
granted Henryk access to the old blood

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:51.040
and it's possible that the miraculous blood granted him life, beyond his years.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.820
Who knows what that can do to a man...

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:59.340
Together, Henryk and Gascoigne were a part of the effort to purge Yharnam of the scourge

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.700
Just two more hunters doing "what hunters must"

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.580
for the good of the city, of course.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:09.180
Gascoigne even found love outside the Church's walls within Ccentral Yharnam

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.600
A woman named Viola.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.400
Blonde and favouring a bright red brooch.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:17.420
Perhaps the jewel was a gift from a hunter.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.980
Imagine being a man of Yharnam during this time

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.980
put your yourself in this city.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.000
As a good yharnamite would,

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.140
you join the nightly hunt with your brothers.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.940
Fighting against the scourge.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.960
You lock your woman and children safely at home

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:36.180
with incense at their doors to ward away the beasts.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:39.180
You fight alongside the Black Church Hunters,

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:43.180
though, this men of the Church are watching you at all times

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:45.180
for any signs of the plague.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:49.440
You fight alongside those who would kill you if they had to.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.580
In time, Viola fell pregnant.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:57.120
Soon after,  Gascoigne left the Healing Church.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:01.260
Perhaps he had something more important to him, now.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:05.220
"Who... are you? I dont know your voice."

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.280
"But I know that smell."

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.620
"Are you a hunter?"

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:12.260
Familly must have pulled him away from the Church

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:14.860
and on the night of our unending hunt

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:18.100
we find this young girl alone in her family's home.

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:20.420
"Please, will you look for my mum?"

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:25.920
"Daddy never came back from the hunt, and she went to find him, but now she's gone, too..."

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:28.840
"I'm all alone... and scared..."

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:32.200
We're looking for a woman with a red brooch

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.320
and a man garbed in black.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:38.700
Imagine being Gascoigne at this point in the story.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.960
An ex-hunter of the Healing Church,

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:46.700
he still wears the tattered black garb that shows how faithfully he served the Church in their hunt.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:51.000
And tonight, the hunt is worse than any night before it.

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:55.020
Tonight, the line between man and beast is blowed.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:02.440
The beast-men of Yharnam cry for death to their ministers

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:05.540
if they see you wearing their minister's garb.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:08.500
This is the exact same thing Gascoigne was wearing.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:12.940
It's unclear exactly what happened in the tomb of Oedon

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:15.020
but here we find Father Gascoigne,

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:18.060
surrounded by the corpses of fellow yharnamites

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:19.680
Hacking them to pieces,

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:22.540
completely lost to his thirst for blood.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:24.700
On a rooftop nearby

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:26.300
we find his wife,

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:27.340
dead.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:35.420
"My mum wears a red jeweled brooch. It's so big and beautiful. You won't miss it."

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:37.520
"Oh, I mustn't forget."

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:41.340
"If you find my mum, give her this music box."

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.320
"It plays one of daddy's favorite songs."

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:48.080
"And when daddy forgets us we play it for him so he remembers."

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.700
"Mum's so silly, running off without it!"

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:54.760
"A small music box recieved from a young Yharnam girl."

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:58.340
"Plays a song shared by her mother and father."

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:02.600
"Inside the lid is a small scrap of paper, perhaps an old message.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:06.080
"Two names can be made out, however faintly,"

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:08.360
"Viola and Gascoigne."

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:10.000
When we play their song,

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.780
the husband recoils an agony

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:14.740
Gascoigne is losing himself to the beastly scourge

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.240
he wants to forget,

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.840
but the music reminds him of his wife,

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:20.320
his children,

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:21.000
his city

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:22.560
his humanity,

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:24.120
his dead wife.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:25.420
His broken city,

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:26.580
his despair.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:29.720
His wife is likely dead as his hand

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:33.900
for she didn't have their music box to remind him of who he was

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:36.340
as she had done many times before.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.860
Gascoigne is beyond saving

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:41.100
and you end his suffering.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:44.800
It almost sound as if his last words are "forgive me".

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:51.540
"Forgive me!"

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:56.860
We don't have the heart to give a child her dead's mother brooch.

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:59.160
Instead, we send her to Oedon Chapel.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:01.560
She can't stay in this house alone

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:05.620
for neither her mother nor her father is coming back for her.

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.480
Better to send her to a safe place.

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:10.680
"Hello miss hunter."

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.780
"Still can't find my mum?"

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.180
"Oh, okay. I can wait."

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.700
"But isn't there something I can do?"

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.980
"Maybe mum and dad are stuck out there,"

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.240
"waiting for me to come and find them."

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:26.580
"What do you think, miss hunter?"

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:29.040
We send her to Oedon Chapel

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:36.020
"Yes okay, thank you miss hunter! I love you almost as much as mum and dad, and grandad!"

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:39.060
She never appears there.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.500
Trace the path she would have taken

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:48.360
imagine this little girl creeping through a sewer filled with crawling corpses and carrion crows.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:55.000
To run past it all and come so close the chapel only to spy this ting at the end of the tunnel.

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:57.300
It eats the little girl

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:59.500
and after your revenge,

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:02.960
you find the bloodied white ribbon upon its remains.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:05.700
"Oh..."

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:10.280
"you haven't by chance... seen my little sister, have you?"

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:13.160
Someone did come back for the little girl

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:18.240
turns out, Gascoigne had two daughters and you just sent one to her death.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:22.920
"I told her to look after the house, but she's run off somewhere."

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:28.400
"She's still quite small, and wears a big white ribbon. Have you seen her out there anywhere?"

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:32.700
"Oh, how did this happen..."

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:35.680
"Why would she ever go outside?"

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:45.120
"At least... I'll have something to remember her by."

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:48.520
The truly sad thing is

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:52.320
a friend of the family was waiting at Oedon tomb arround this time.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:55.640
The one the littlest daughter calls "grandad".

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:58.220
He could've met the youngest daughter there

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:00.900
had the pig not consumed her in the tunnel.

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:05.260
Instead, Henryk goes mad here in this place

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:08.360
Perhaps he discovered that someone killed his friend

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:12.320
or perhaps, since the littlest daughter calls him "grandad",

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.800
he discovered the corpse of his daughter,

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:15.700
Viola.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:21.960
"Perfect timing"

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:24.380
"I must warn you..."

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:28.980
"...not to go near the tomb below Oedon Chapel in the Cathedral Ward."

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:30.660
"Henryk,"

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:34.720
"an old hunter, has gone mad."

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:38.880
"And he's my mark..."

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.680
When we arrive, we're already too late.

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:48.160
As with Gascoigne, loss pushes Henryk over the edge.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:51.140
We've seen that hunters turn into terrible beasts,

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:53.240
so the hunter must become the hunted.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:01.480
"That wasn't necessary of ya."

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:03.100
But you have my thanks."

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:07.660
"We made it with our lives... You're not bad at all."

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:12.440
"You must have killed Gascoigne as well then."

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:19.100
"He was falling apart... I'm sure it had to be done."

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.800
But try to keep your hands clean..."

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:25.700
"The Hunter should hunt Beasts."

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:29.380
"Leave the hunting of Hunters, to me."

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:35.580
Gascoigne killed his wife.

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:37.020
We killed Gascoigne.

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:40.740
Henryk tried to kill us, so Eileen killed Henryk.

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:44.400
The last surviving daughter throws herself off a ledge

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:46.660
upon receiving her sister's bloodied ribbon.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.880
And the bloodline of Gascoigne ends here.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:55.560
However, somewhere in another hunt, perhaps,

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:57.980
you never spoke to the littlest daughter.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:00.440
She never went looking for her parents,

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:02.780
she never travelled down this tunnel.

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:06.560
She stayed home until her sister returned

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:09.120
and they huddled together until morning came.

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:13.820
"I won't be afraid. I know, I do."

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:16.300
"The morning always comes."

